PARSFILE
#FullDataName Events`B. Maintain Constant Speed`Transient Response Times
#CheckBox1 0    
#CheckBox2 0    
#CheckBox3 0    
#CheckBox4 0    
#CheckBox5 1    
#CheckBox6 1    
#CheckBox7 0    
#CheckBox8 0    

#RingCtrl0 >
#RingCtrl10 1
#RingCtrl11 1
*NAME1 t_event
*VALUE1 time_settle
*SPEED speed_in_mph


! Reset all open-loop control clocks by setting parameters to current time
TSTART_T_EVENT = T ; ! 2014
T_EVENT_START = T ; ! legacy
TSTART_BRAKES = T ;
TSTART_STEER_TQ = T ;
TSTART_F_BRAKE_PEDAL = T ;
TSTART_PBK_CON = T ;
TSTART_CLUTCH = T ;
TSTART_GEAR = T ;
TSTART_SPEED_CTRL = T ;
TSTART_STEER = T ;
TSTART_THROTTLE = T ;
TSTART_TRANS = T ;
TSTART_WIND = T ;
OPT_INIT_CONFIG 0
OPT_INIT_PATH 0
OPT_INIT_SPEED 0
INSTALL_DRIVER_SPEED_CONTROLLER 2014
Opt_SC 3
OPT_SC 3
SPEED_TARGET_COMBINE ADD
SPEED_TARGET_CONSTANT 0
SPEED_TARGET_S_CONSTANT speed_in_mph
OPT_SC_ENGINE_BRAKING 0
PARSFILE Control\Throttle\Throttle_768d3744-c109-4ff7-a65b-3b0bea560117.par
#BlueLink10 Control: Throttle (Open Loop)`Constant: 0` Constant` , Miscellaneous`Throttle_768d3744-c109-4ff7-a65b-3b0bea560117

DEFINE_EVENT t_event > time_settle ; Events\Events_4c485117-53e8-4b01-b982-a673f7fc25b8.par
#BlueLink0 Events`C. Slowly Increasing Steer` Transient Response Times` , Events`Events_4c485117-53e8-4b01-b982-a673f7fc25b8


#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#The "speed_in_mph" parameter is pasted into the yellow field for the Constant Target Speed. (Even though the field is too small to display it, it is there.)
#
#An open-loop throttle control is linked here to "turn-off" the open loop throttle setting from the previous event.
#
#The target speed is maintained for a settling time, to reach steady state.
#
#The checkbox to reset the control clocks is checked so t_event can be used to monitor the time elapsed since this event began.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: Events; { Transient Response Times } B. Maintain Constant Speed
#Library : Events
#DataSet : B. Maintain Constant Speed
